 D-002; user choice "All outer corners"): every outer-boundary corner is `Corner_End`, Corner_1's footprint with both arm ends closed and rounded (Blender, same `WallBrick.blend`/`.fbx`, `Corner_End.prefab` from Corner_1.prefab with only the mesh replaced), so a lowered gate beside it shows a rounded end; and each wall quadrant and door slot stands on a `FloorBase` square that reaches floor, walls and gates but stops a quarter quadrant short of open void, so gaps between units read dark instead of showing the background. Reopened again for the user's gate and corner request (D-003, D-004; answers "Approve gate ends" and "Reshape Corner_End"): each gate is closed by `Door_End`, Door_1x1's cross-section with one rounded end (Blender, same `WallBrick.blend`/`.fbx`, `Door_End.prefab` from Door_1x1.prefab with only the mesh replaced), on its first and last slot, with two half-length ends on a one-slot gate; the whole gate still sinks and rises as one span. `Corner_End`'s outer side became one large quarter-round arc as in the reference, since no supplied corner has one. Supplied FBX files and the Wall, corner and door prefabs are unchanged. See [Environment Layout](docs/Environment-Layout.md). Task `TASK-20260927-123500933-c1e67965-environment-runs-gate-motion`. |
 | One startup loading screen in Init (DEC-140) | User request of 2026-09-27 ("ilk açılışta her şey hazır olana kadar sadece bir kez loading ... level geçişleri dahil loading olmayacak"), with the approved option of merging Loading into Init. `StartupLoader` (`Runtime/Startup`, an `OnitySceneInitiator` that replaces Onity's bootstrap initiator on Init) shows `StartupLoadingView` from Init's first frame, waits for `ProjectContext.ReadyTask` (level JSON, shapes, player save), loads Hub additively behind the screen, makes it the active scene, waits for Hub's `SceneContext.ReadyTask` (Home bound) plus one frame for Home's first layout, then unloads Init. A failed project scope is not rethrown: Hub shows Home with the level button disabled (AC-10) rather than leaving the player on the loading screen. The bar only moves forward: `StartupProgress` maps the project wait (time-based, below 1) and then the Hub load onto one value; the percentage text changes only when the whole percent changes (ZString). Layout follows the real game's startup screen (user reference): Home's `bg_home_screen`, a centred "Color Block Jam" title and a rounded navy bar with the percentage near the bottom (`UI/Startup/StartupLoading.uxml`). `LoadingPanelSettings` now uses the runtime theme, Expand matching and sorting order 100, so it draws above Hub's panel (0) and blocks presses while Hub builds. `Loading.unity` is deleted and removed from Build Settings, and the scene-flow profile names no Loading scene with routing through it off, so Hub, Game, Restart and next level never show a loading screen. Replaces DEC-98's "Loading appears only for actual loading". Ad-hoc change without a task contract. |
